CVE-2026-48019 / PKSA-zwc5-qtrz-zm1n / GHSA-5vg9-5847-vvmq
"Laravel CRLF injection in default email rule"

illuminate/validation is flagged as vulnerable for EVERY tag matching
>=9.0.0,<10.0.0 | >=10.0.0,<11.0.0 | >=11.0.0,<12.0.0 (and 12.x below
12.60.0, 13.x below 13.10.0) -- there is no patched 11.x release to
require instead. Backports the upstream fix (illuminate/validation commit
297cff9c69885b1a9125ee4f26f77ef570abb2b6, "port fix", released in 12.60.0)
into ValidatesAttributes::validateEmail(): reject any input containing a
CR or LF character before it reaches the rest of the email validation
chain, closing the header-injection path into outbound mail.

Paired with the "ignore-id": ["PKSA-zwc5-qtrz-zm1n"] entry in
composer.json's audit policy -- that entry exists so Composer's resolver
doesn't refuse this advisory-flagged (but now patched) tag and fall back
to an unreleased -dev branch instead. Ignoring the advisory without this
patch would be masking the CVE rather than fixing it.

--- a/Concerns/ValidatesAttributes.php	2026-08-04 23:35:02
+++ b/Concerns/ValidatesAttributes.php	2026-08-04 23:35:02
@@ -909,6 +909,10 @@
     public function validateEmail($attribute, $value, $parameters)
     {
         if (! is_string($value) && ! (is_object($value) && method_exists($value, '__toString'))) {
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        if (preg_match('/[\r\n]/', (string) $value) > 0) {
             return false;
         }

